From: OpenBMC X570D4I-2T port <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] redfish: Systems EthernetInterfaces from NIC inventory

Serve read-only /redfish/v1/Systems/system/EthernetInterfaces from
xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.NetworkInterface inventory objects.

Upstream bmcweb has no Systems-level EthernetInterfaces: ethernet.hpp is
the BMC's own network stack (Managers/bmc) and hypervisor_system.hpp is
the IBM PHYP contract, expecting writable xyz.openbmc_project.Network.*
objects under /xyz/openbmc_project/network/hypervisor. Neither can
describe the HOST's NICs on a board where the BMC simply knows what is
installed. phosphor-dbus-interfaces already defines the right inventory
shape (Item.NetworkInterface, a MACAddress string plus an optional
produced_by association), so render that, exactly the way storage.hpp
and fabric_adapters.hpp render Item.Storage / Item.FabricAdapter.

On this board the publisher is p2a-inventory-monitor, which reads the
host X550-AT2 port MACs out of the board FRU EEPROM (i2c7/0x57,
0x3F90/0x3F98) — so the collection answers with the host powered off,
which is the case provisioning stacks (Ironic, Metal3, metal-boot) care
about: they enumerate exactly this collection to discover boot MACs.
The routes carry no board-specific knowledge.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Also link EthernetInterfaces from the ComputerSystem resource alongside
its Storage/Memory/FabricAdapters siblings (non-multi-host block only,
matching those).

--- a/redfish-core/src/redfish.cpp
+++ b/redfish-core/src/redfish.cpp
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@
 #include "storage_controller.hpp"
 #include "switch_port.hpp"
